e up dormant desires from Mithras, but still going from the 4th generation to the 6th generation would be something that would bother me to no end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T17:34:37-07:00","id":1541617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541018-best-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1541537#post1541537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was going by His write up in Children of the Night and they left his physical attributes unknown and went with the description that his strength and stamina were unearthly. I'm thinking that he was Strength:8, Stamina:8, and Dexterity was at least 7.</div> </div> </div> </div>His physical statistics are there in the manual. You simply have to check the sheet of Jalan-Ajav.<br /> Which means Strength 8, Dexterity 7, Stamina 8, as you guessed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-05-2024, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T17:50:55-07:00","id":1541619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541018-best-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1541516#post1541516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I demand a rematch between the two in the squared circle and we get Jim Ross and Jerry Lawler announce it.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>stats at hand it's not possible for Theo to beat Karsh. Karsh/Ajav has one of the most balanced and insane character sheets in Vampire the Masquerade. He has a pure pysichal combat-specialized sheet, and by god, he does it well. To get something better, you'd have to look at Menele, Enkidu, or Tariq.<br /> <br /> That said, Theo has an excellent sheet, easily that of an elder, and it's also extremely balanced for an all-around fighter with a lot of versatility. He's a couple of steps below Karsh, but still remarkable nonetheless.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rab