t-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1541640#post1541640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ahh if only we knew a Turkish-Mongolian Gangrel, prone to diablerie and who had access to a 4th generation throat to develop that power</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I never much cared for that &quot;secret&quot; unlike the theory that Hardelstadt was Jurgen.<br /> <br /> What is really added by them being split?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T09:17:05-07:00","id":1541687,"title":"","content":"It does seem to overly complicate things by having Karsh and Jalan just being fragments of a older more powerful monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T10:52:55-07:00","id":1541688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541018-best-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1541687#post1541687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does seem to overly complicate things by having Karsh and Jalan just being fragments of a older more powerful monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>The alternatives really aren't less convoluted.<br /> <br /> On one hand you have the possibility of a single vampire with multiple alternate identities, who's managed to work himself into the highest echelons of three separate sects which all mutually hate each other, running around the whole-ass planet like it's the end of Mrs. Doubtfire while successfully keeping the wool over every other elder's and methuselah's eyes.<br /> <br /> It's certainly <i>possible</i>. Towards the end of the TC game in which I played a Tremere, three out of the five PC's (myself included) never actually had to daysleep, because we all had teleportation/rapid transport powers and abused the hell out of the whole &quot;the Earth is round and it's always nighttime somewhere&quot; thing. The Lasombra and Setite had multiple havens around the globe in strategic locations; the Lasombra shadowstepped between them and the Setite just teleported around with Path of Praapti. My Tremere was a master necromancer, towards the end of the chronicle spent more time in the Shadowlands than the Skinlands (being a Red Lister does that), and had a network of ferryman to transport him between various nihils across the world.<br /> <br /> Those characters were older than either Karsh or Jalan by a matter of decades, but higher generation (the Setite was 7th, the Lasombra and myself were 6th when this was going on). Which brings me back to the Gangrel: neither of these characters have powers which on their face allow for the kind of mobility our PC's had, as there's no combination of Celerity, Fortitude, and Protean that allow for <i>hypersonic</i> earth melded travel of which I'm aware -- and we can discard the idea of supersonic passenger jets, from that kind of thing being traceable as well as new. So possible, but not likely.<br /> <br /> On the other, they may well just be two different vampires with no relation to another...and that notion just falls completely flat. <i>Maybe</i> they were specifically conditioned and brought up by Qarakh to be identical, working all sects against one another? but that means they are related, thereby negating the premise. There's no other feasible explanation for how two unrelated vampires, even of the same clan, would have the same age, same generation, same attributes, and work themselves into identical roles for opposing sects with sect affiliation being the only point of divergence.<br /> <br /> We gotta go with Occam's razor here. Counterintuitive though it may be, Qarakh undergoing vampiric mitosis really is the simplest explanation, even if it leaves us wondering why he would even do it in the first place.<br /> <br /> My pet theory with absolutely no substantiating evidence, is Qarakh ate two low-gen vampires in rapid succession, one of which while possessed by a pagan deity (and getting partially Kupala'ed in the process). Qarakh could not have been anything older than ancilla-age at the time, and while low-gen himself, that's simply not enough time to have developed an elder's force of will. Aajav (who remember was Qarakh's mortal brother) allowed himself to be eaten to consolidate blood, but Alexander certainly didn't.<br /> <br /> One way or the other, that's a mountain of mental trauma in very short order. Successfully assimilating a two thousand-year-old, fourth-generation, Ventrue's soul probably isn't even the least of it on a personal level. I suspect vampire mitosis was the coping mechanism: what was left of Alexander got shunted off into &quot;Karsh&quot; as an alter to protect &quot;Jalan&quot;. Or to put it another way, Karsh is the Therese to Jalan's Jeanette.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T11:27:32-07:00","id":1541690,"title":"","content":"Or you could ignore their identical stats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T12:39:02-07:00","id":1541694,"title":"","content":"It's makes for an interesting debate of Karsh &amp; Jalan being semi independent fragments of a high level Protean power that the original Gangrel used to play off both sects and everyone else to suit there own needs. As crazy as it sounds that this might be the best answer for this mess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T15:10:01-07:00","id":1541704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541018-best-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1541690#post1541690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could ignore their identical stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really doubt &quot;they just copy/pasted the stat block&quot; (the easiest, first, and most rational explanation for this) really applies on this. The writers invented an entirely new Camarilla title and rank, unique to <i>Children of the Night</i>, just for Karsh to be parallel to Jalan as Seraph -- at the same time as making both backstories, ages, and generations (far bigger deals than any individual attribute, ability, discipline, background, virtue, or derived stat) identical.<br /> <br /> The newness and uniqueness of the title &quot;Warlord of the Camarilla&quot; is noteworthy in and of itself, as in previous (and subsequent) books the responsibility to marshal and lead Camarilla in times of open conflict simply fell to Justicars, Archons, and Princes respectively depending on scope and severity of the conflict. It's simply redundant, and only exists to draw attention to Karsh and his role within the sect. And just two years after <i>Children of the Night</i>, <i>Midnight Siege</i> revised/retconned the title into the more open-ended (and not unique to Karsh) &quot;Dux Bellorum&quot;, to which <i>any</i> Camarilla vampire of sufficient and relevant rank can be temporarily elevated.<br /> <br /> These are all hints to draw attention to the similarities of the two, for readers to infer (without providing hard answers) some relationship between Karsh and Jalan-Aajav. Whatever that relationship might be. Bear in mind this is the same writing team that gave us <i>Clanbook: Giovanni</i>, noteworthy here for making the Capuchin's character write-up specifically seven paragraphs just so they could spell &quot;Lazarus&quot; with the first letter for each -- metatextual hints to the truth of in-universe mysteries is absolutely their wheelhouse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541018-best-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1541694#post1541694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's makes for an interesting debate of Karsh &amp; Jalan being semi independent fragments of a high level Protean power that the original Gangrel used to play off both sects and everyone else to suit there own needs. As crazy as it sounds that this might be the best answer for this mess.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least for the purposes of my own pet theory, it's more fitting (and tragic) for Qarakh to have met Final Death in the act of vampire mitosis, leaving Karsh and Jalan-Aajav fully-fledged and independent Cainites in his place. It's not one (or two) vampires playing Camarilla and Sabbat against one another for personal motive, but two &quot;childer&quot; in all but the Embrace going their separate ways and acting as dictated by the personality fragments with which they were left. Thus they're not necessarily enemies, at each other's throats, or have an antagonistic &quot;there can be only one&quot; relationship -- they've just had separate unlife paths which ironically left them in comparable places across sect boundaries.<br /> <br /> It might bend the published rules of Dual Form a bit, but mechanics have always taken second seat to story in VtM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-07-2024, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T15:24:56-07:00","id":1541705,"title":"","content":"I should add Myca Vykos as a good rival or threat to deal with. You have 1,000+ year old 6th generation fiend that is highly intelligent and adaptable to changing conditions who like Mr. Sinister is creepy and detached and has a considerable amount of personal power to handle most dangers easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T18:54:58-07:00","id":1541718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541018-best-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1541704#post1541704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really doubt &quot;they just copy/pasted the stat block&quot; (the easiest, first, and most rational explanation for this) really applies on this. The writers invented an entirely new Camarilla title and rank, unique to <i>Children of the Night</i>, just for Karsh to be parallel to Jalan as Seraph -- at the same time as making both backstories, ages, and generations (far bigger deals than any individual attribute, ability, discipline, background, virtue, or derived stat) identical.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're born a century apart.<br /> <br /> Jalan is Mongolian.<br /> <br /> Karsh is Turkish.<br /> <br /> That's the biggest argument they're not the same person split into two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T19:08:23-07:00","id":1541719,"title":"","content":"If I had to say who the best antagonists in all of V:TM are, you're not going to be surprised by my picks. You may not agree but no one will be surprised by my picks.<br /> <br /> <b>Modius</b> and <b>Juggler</b>.<br /> <br /> Yes, the original characters from FORGED IN STEEL.<br /> <br /> 1. Modius is the perfect &quot;starter prince&quot; for player characters to be up against because he's a guy who is a hundred+ years old, bordering two hundred but he's half-insane and a pathetic shell of a Camarilla stooge. He's the worst Prince in the Camarilla but he's STILL a Prince and that means he has power, money, and authority. It's just that there's a reasonable chance your Neonate PCs COULD overthrow him if they wanted to. If they did, they could get their own city. The only problem is that city is Gary, Indiana. However, that's still better than just about any other lick their age might have.<br /> <br /> Modius is a perfect example of how old age can drive an Elder insane and what will eventually result in either torpor or wassail. Maybe Modius will turn against the PCs because of Allicia, maybe he'll do it because of paranoia about them being Anarchs, or maybe the PCs will do it because he's such an easy target. There's a lot to do here and yet I kind of like the idea that he's a survivor and in the 'canon' timeline, he outlives Lodin and many other stronger princes.<br /> <br /> I'm very fond of the classic &quot;Beauty and the Beast' story where the PCs rescue Allicia from his blood bond too.<br /> <br /> 2. Juggler is a great antagonist because he's the first Anarch in the entire setting and sets the mood for the sect. Just as Modius is a pathetic has been of an Elder, Juggler is the perfect example of the Anarch sell out. He talks a great deal about overthrowing the man and being a trendy modern rebel but he wears expensive suits and he keeps his childe enslaved by a blood bond--just like Modius.<br /> <br /> The thing is, I don't think he was meant to represent the Anarchs as a whole. No, the PCs were meant to overthrow him and be the Anarch he was never meant to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T08:43:09-07:00","id":1541739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541018-best-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1541718#post1541718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're born a century apart.<br /> <br /> Jalan is Mongolian.<br /> <br /> Karsh is Turkish.<br /> <br /> That's the biggest argument they're not the same person split into two.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Karsh <i>claims</i> to be a Turk. In the same way he <i>claims</i> to have been a janissary and fought in a battle three hundred years before the janissaries' founding, was embraced after his betrayal by Murad I a hundred years before Murad I was even born, returned as a neonate to lead a janissary revolt against a sultan who hadn't even been born yet, to install the Koprulu dynasty three hundred years before the Koprulu dynasty was even founded, and joined the Camarilla before the Anarch Revolt had even started.<br /> <br /> The Battle of Manzikert happened in 1071. The Janissary corps was not founded until the reign of Murad I (i.e. no earlier than 1362), and Murad I was Sultan from 1362-1389. There was a Janissary revolt against a Sultan, and that Sultan was executed after which the Koprulu dynasty came to power -- but the Sultan was Ibrahim the Mad, it happened in 1648, and Koprulu Mehmed would not be appointed Grand Vizier until 1656.<br /> <br /> I won't even get into how there's only one way Karsh could have been a Janissary in the first place, and that sole way fundamentally contradicts his own narrative even if the timeline somehow fit. At least, not yet. I just want to point that out and put a pin in it, should this conversation continue.<br /> <br /> And besides that...indeed, Turks and Mongols. Two groups with no shared ethnic, cultural, or geographic origin, who didn't culturally assimilate with one another and cross-pollinate across three empires spanning eastern Europe, central Asia, and the Middle East during the eleventh through fourteenth Centuries. Funny how that's <i>exactly</i> the span of time we're expected to just...ignore...to buy Karsh's narrative of his origins.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the only externally and independently established part of Karsh's backstory is that he rode in westward expansionary raids with the &quot;Tatars&quot;. A term used interchangeably with &quot;Mongol&quot;, particularly in the context of the Golden Horde -- in and of itself a Turco-Mongol empire.<br /> <br /> Karsh claiming to be a Turk is basically the single most meaningless part of his entire narrative. If anything it reinforces the similarities between his and Jalan's origin stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T14:43:49-07:00","id":1541749,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the two being alternate identities of the same vampire because it doesn't depend on the involvement of a hidden methuselah using outlandish high-level powers. The two run in different circles, probably with no mutual acquaintances between them, which lends itself to a &quot;has anyone ever seen them in the same room?&quot; scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T20:12:11-07:00","id":1541760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541018-best-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1541739#post1541739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Karsh <i>claims</i> to be a Turk. In the same way he <i>claims</i> to have been a janissary and fought in a battle three hundred years before the janissaries' founding, was embraced after his betrayal by Murad I a hundred years before Murad I was even born, returned as a neonate to lead a janissary revolt against a sultan who hadn't even been born yet, to install the Koprulu dynasty three hundred years before the Koprulu dynasty was even founded, and joined the Camarilla before the Anarch Revolt had even started.<br /> <br /> The Battle of Manzikert happened in 1071. The Janissary corps was not founded until the reign of Murad I (i.e. no earlier than 1362), and Murad I was Sultan from 1362-1389. There was a Janissary revolt against a Sultan, and that Sultan was executed after which the Koprulu dynasty came to power -- but the Sultan was Ibrahim the Mad, it happened in 1648, and Koprulu Mehmed would not be appointed Grand Vizier until 1656.<br /> <br /> I won't even get into how there's only one way Karsh could have been a Janissary in the first place, and that sole way fundamentally contradicts his own narrative even if the timeline somehow fit. At least, not yet. I just want to point that out and put a pin in it, should this conversation continue.<br /> <br /> And besides that...indeed, Turks and Mongols. Two groups with no shared ethnic, cultural, or geographic origin, who didn't culturally assimilate with one another and cross-pollinate across three empires spanning eastern Europe, central Asia, and the Middle East during the eleventh through fourteenth Centuries. Funny how that's <i>exactly</i> the span of time we're expected to just...ignore...to buy Karsh's narrative of his origins.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the only externally and independently established part of Karsh's backstory is that he rode in westward expansionary raids with the &quot;Tatars&quot;. A term used interchangeably with &quot;Mongol&quot;, particularly in the context of the Golden Horde -- in and of itself a Turco-Mongol empire.<br /> <br /> Karsh claiming to be a Turk is basically the single most meaningless part of his entire narrative. If anything it reinforces the similarities between his and Jalan's origin stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean your argument seems to be, &quot;They can't possibly be what they claim to be because that would mean they weren't the same person.&quot;<br /> <br /> I guess I prefer their claimed backstories to the idea they're splits of the same Methusaleh.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541018-best-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1541749#post1541749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of the two being alternate identities of the same vampire because it doesn't depend on the involvement of a hidden methuselah using outlandish high-level powers. The two run in different circles, probably with no mutual acquaintances between them, which lends itself to a &quot;has anyone ever seen them in the same room?&quot; scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I could easily see both using body doubles like Nosferatu or Tzimisce too or Possession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T13:44:02-07:00","id":1541798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541018-best-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1541760#post1541760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean your argument seems to be, &quot;They can't possibly be what they claim to be because that would mean they weren't the same person.&quot;<br /> <br /> I guess I prefer their claimed backstories to the idea they're splits of the same Methusaleh.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but no, just no.<br /> <br /> It was a counterpoint to your allegation that their backstories are irreconcilable, and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar431_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"431\" data-vbnamecard=\"431\">Theodrim</a> clearly shows that Karsh's backstory is bullshit.<br /> <br /> While it doesn't means they're secretly the same person, it does demonstrate that the evidence otherwise is false.<br /> <br /> By the w