distinct people, but have this confusion be a deliberate red herring for anyone looking close enough to even notice the similarities in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it means that writers did bad research.<br /> <br /> Not that it was a secret clue.<br /> <br /> It also is a shame to get rid of a Turkish general to combine it with a guy who isn't even the same ethnicity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T15:19:58-07:00","id":1541806,"title":"","content":"With long running series in general, you are going to get things that contradict earlier lore.<br /> <br /> Such as NCIS where we get the story of how Gibbs and Doctor Mallard met and he is aware if Gibbs first wife.<br /> <br /> It contradicts the fact that in season 3 that the Doctor didn't know about the first wife at all and just knew that Agent Gibbs had been married and divorced 3 times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T16:02:21-07:00","id":1541809,"title":"","content":"I should note that I fully expect them to lean into the Karsh and Jalan are the same thing theory if they ever do decide to revisit the plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T16:11:54-07:00","id":1541811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541018-best-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1541801#post1541801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it means that writers did bad research.<br /> <br /> Not that it was a secret clue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, the same writers literally pointed out in the same entry his supposed backstory is full of contradictions and inconsistencies. You're supposing they did bad research, then went out of their way to point out their own research was bad, and instead of scrap the entry and write something else put it to print <i>anyways</i>?<br /> <br /> A clue cannot be a &quot;secret clue&quot; when the authors specifically point it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> It also is a shame to get rid of a Turkish general to combine it with a guy who isn't even the same ethnicity. </div> </div> </div>You're gonna shit if you ever read about the origins of the Oghuz Turks (of which the Seljuk were one tribe), having said this. They're literally just west- and southward migration of Eurasian Steppe peoples that occurred between the Eighth and Eleventh Centuries; they just happened mass-convert to Islam during that time, and the Seljuks continued migrating southward into Persia.<br /> <br /> Hell, if you want to make hay about Jalan-Aajav here, the Mongol Empire itself was majority Turkic. Saying he's a &quot;Mongol&quot; absent any other context means as much as saying Karsh is a &quot;Turk&quot;. Which is, let me restate my point, exactly frig-all thanks to the overwhelming amount of cultural cross-pollination and assimilation that occurred between those two peoples, especially at this time in history as the Mongol Empire had heavily Turkicizied by the mid-13th Century. There's nothing substantive there to make an ethnic or cultural distinction between the two.<br /> <br /> Even accounting for the book itself stating that's merely a rumor about his mortal origin and age, which he's apparently never confirmed or denied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T16:49:30-07:00","id":1541818,"title":"","content":"Alright.<br /> <br /> In any case, it seems like what they were alluding to even if I don't care for it. Point conceded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T16:31:00-07:00","id":1541890,"title":"","content":"One minor question that always intrigued me is Lambach Ruthhaven a direct childe or grand childer of the eldest? And besides him being a natural survivor makes him worthy of such protection of the founder of there clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T16:51:17-07:00","id":1541893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541018-best-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1541890#post1541890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One minor question that always intrigued me is Lambach Ruthhaven a direct childe or grand childer of the eldest? And besides him being a natural survivor makes him worthy of such protection of the founder of there clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought Dracula captured Lambach and his sire, forced Lambach to embrace him, and then diablerized Lambach's sire.<br /> <br /> I always thought Lambach was always someone who the Eldest enjoyed toying with versus favoring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T16:56:00-07:00","id":1541896,"title":"","content":"It's said that Dracula did capture Lambach and Tabak and made sure to get embraced by one of them. But that could be not what really happened at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T17:55:13-07:00","id":1541902,"title":"","content":"While the most known story about Lambach is the Dracula debacle, he shows up a number of times in circumstances that are contradictory between them.<br /> <br /> His real nature and identity is purposefully left uncertain, so he may be anything between 4th and 6th Generation, with varying degrees of courage and overall competency, and he can also be one of the pieces of the Eldest.<br /> <br /> The more you play Lambach as a survivalist without much courage or ambition, the more likely that he's &quot;high&quot; Gen and an unwilling instrument of the Eldest. The more you want Lambach to be ambitious and/or powerful, the more he's a low Gen playing from behind this facade.<br /> <br /> Personally I like to change my take on him from one game to another, and while I'm not sure I'd call him an antagonist, I do like the character a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T18:45:57-07:00","id":1541904,"title":"","content":"He is definitely interesting to say the least with such contradictions about him. I do think that there's way more behind him then what most kindred think and that he is playing a long con and putting on a facade of weakness and only the eldest sees it and admires the work that his possible childe is doing and that the others would be scared if the mask would slip.<br /> <br /> Maybe he is akin to Keyser Souze from The Usual Suspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-11-2024, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T22:34:59-07:00","id":1541913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541018-best-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1541902#post1541902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the most known story about Lambach is the Dracula debacle, he shows up a number of times in circumstances that are contradictory between them.<br /> <br /> His real nature and identity is purposefully left uncertain, so he may be anything between 4th and 6th Generation, with varying degrees of courage and overall competency, and he can also be one of the pieces of the Eldest.<br /> <br /> The more you play Lambach as a survivalist without much courage or ambition, the more likely that he's &quot;high&quot; Gen and an unwilling instrument of the Eldest. The more you want Lambach to be ambitious and/or powerful, the more he's a low Gen playing from behind this facade.<br /> <br /> Personally I like to change my take on him from one game to another, and while I'm not sure I'd call him an antagonist, I do like the character a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny, I play him as an absolutely cowardly and sniveling 5th Generation.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat underestimate him, of course, and he thus trashes whoever tries to take his blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T10:07:47-07:00","id":1541927,"title":"","content":"That would work as Lambach is viewed as cowardly and weak by most and it wouldn't violate lore. Just as the idea that he is putting on a facade and is playing a long game and my idea of him being like Virgil Kant/Keyser Souze would also work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T18:53:32-07:00","id":1541941,"title":"","content":"He works wonderfully both ways. The only thing he isn't is a pushover if things get real, but he definitely is, or appears to be, while they remain as threat.<br /> <br /> Coward Lambach isn't just a comic relief, he's an opportunity to put your PCs in contact with an Elder/Methuselah that isn't threatening, so you can get all sorts of interactions that would be hard to build around most old vampires.<br /> <br /> And while he's cautious and paranoid, he can be open to be vulnerable in ways other vampires can't, because he does have enough power to take care of himself, and he doesn't have a reputation to protect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T19:49:11-07:00","id":1541943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541018-best-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1541893#post1541893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Dracula captured Lambach and his sire, forced Lambach to embrace him, and then diablerized Lambach's sire.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the story from <i>Children of the Inquisition</i>. I think later books may have called his relationship to Tabak into question and implied he was a methuselah enacting some master plan (at least I hope it was books and not just fanon). Since the original is one of the game's best-written products in my opinion, I've always treated it as the correct version.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T14:59:32-07:00","id":1542000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541018-best-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1541943#post1541943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the story from <i>Children of the Inquisition</i>. I think later books may have called his relationship to Tabak into question and implied he was a methuselah enacting some master plan (at least I hope it was books and not just fanon). Since the original is one of the game's best-written products in my opinion, I've always treated it as the correct version.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tabak is officially a 6th generation Vampire, childe of Tabak Ruthven and sire of Danika Ruthven (Lair of the hidden, Timizce Novel Dark Ages)<br /> <br /> <br /> There is a large Tzimisce family, the Ruthvens, who descend from a mysterious Lord Ruthven. The Ruthvens have always been the guardians of the Antediluvian. Damek Ruthven was the Voivode among Voivodes, and in his castle, a part of the Tzimisce Antediluvian was kept.<br /> <br /> In <i>Beckett's Jyhad Diary</i>, Lambach is located in the Cayman Islands. But when Beckett meets Dracula, Dracula tells him that his sire has been imprisoned for a very long time in the castle of Poenari. If Dracula's sire is locked away in Poenari, it cannot be Lambach. But if it were Lambach, who is the vampire in Poenari Castle?<br /> <br /> I gave my answer a while ago. Many ancient Tzimisce tend to transcend their individual identities. Yorak was one with the Cathedral of Flesh, Byelobog had become the Pripet marshes, Demendeh transformed into a Virus, the Dragon was fused into Tzimisce and implanted in Vykos, Kartarirya sought to remold itself into a creature capable of existing in multiple states of awareness simultaneously.<br /> <br /> The Eldest itself transcended its individuality, being able to reincarnate in any Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> <i>Beckett's Jyhad Diary</i> also showed us that not only can the Antediluvian incarnate in any Tzimisce, but it can also absorb and rebirth entire vampires. Although Ilyas Cel Frumos had died, he was reborn in the flesh of Tzimisce and now lives under New York, just as Tzimisce once reincarnated in the Dragon after the battle with Samiel. Lambach himself, in the diary, sometimes calls himself the child, grandchild, and great-grandchild of Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> I believe that Lord Ruthven simply did what all the others did: he transcended his individuality, able to manifest in any of his direct descendants, in a lesser version of the Antediluvian\u2019s most characteristic power. Sometimes Lambach is a fifth-generation Methuselah, and sometimes a fourth-generation Methuselah, depending on whether Lord Ruthven manifests in him. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T15:18:00-07:00","id":1542002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541018-best-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1541688#post1541688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The alternatives really aren't less convoluted.<br /> <br /> On one hand you have the possibility of a single vampire with multiple alternate identities, who's managed to work himself into the highest echelons of three separate sects which all mutually hate each other, running around the whole-ass planet like it's the end of Mrs. Doubtfire while successfully keeping the wool over every other elder's and methuselah's eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well counting that the other Seraphs are Elimelech and Djuah, both agents of the True Black Hand infiltrated into the Sabbat, and that the First Seraph was a Baali infiltrated into the True Black Hand to infiltrate the Fake Black Hand...it is not that Ajaav stands out all that much.<br /> <br /> These high-level infiltrations are anything but rare. Vitel posed as a Ventrue for 50 years without anyone suspecting a thing, and after Lodin, he was the most powerful prince in the United States. Kemintiri pretended to be a Justicar for a lifetime (as well as hundreds of other people), and even Archons and Templars have told us that the Inner Circle of the Camarilla contains at least one Sabbat infiltrator.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ah, another fun fact people forget.<br /> <br /> From Children of the Nights<br /> <br /> Karsh<br /> <i>&quot;Speculation aside, <b>Cainite historians tell tales of an auspicious meeting immediately preceding the close of the 15th century between undead hand and unbroken will. It was there that Hassan al-Samhir pledged eternal fealty to an immortal calling himself Hardestadt of Ventrue, leader of men and monsters</b>, a being whose words swayed nations \u2014 and bearer of an uncanny intellect, who knew words would not always be enough. Thus was the Warlord of the Camarilla born.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Ajaav<br /> <i>&quot;What is known is that, <b>sometime shortly after the 15th century\u2019s dawning, Jalan\u2019s westward wanderings brought him into contact with another of his kind </b>\u2014 a<b>n ancient creature who had carefully concealed his presence during centuries of Teutonic worship</b>, fi tful in the Sleep of Ages within a newborn Orthodox cathedral, <b>hidden in plain sight beneath a riverside hamlet that bore his very name.</b> There, astride the banks of the wine-dark Timis in the Romanian fi sherman\u2019s village of <b>Lugoj</b>, the warrior fi rst heard the tale of the Antediluvians. There, amidst the fi re-fl ower dance of death, he tasted the forbidden fruit his brothers called Amaranth. And there, kneeling in homage to the priests and sorcerers of the manus nigrum, Jalan, onetime-terror of the East, rejoined the great game for power at any price.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> So, these two bastards, more or less at the same time, meet one the founder of the Sabbat, the other the founder of the Camarilla, and become their main generals. What luck! What a coincidence!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-12-2024, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T18:48:52-07:00","id":1542012,"title":"","content":"Funny how the war of the ages works out in such odd ways Undead Rabbit.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T15:54:00-07:00","id":1542076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541018-best-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1542002#post1542002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well counting that the other Seraphs are Elimelech and Djuah, both agents of the True Black Hand infiltrated into the Sabbat, and that the First Seraph was a Baali infiltrated into the True Black Hand to infiltrate the Fake Black Hand...it is not that Ajaav stands out all that much.<br /> <br /> These high-level infiltrations are anything but rare. Vitel posed as a Ventrue for 50 years without anyone suspecting a thing, and after Lodin, he was the most powerful prince in the United States. Kemintiri pretended to be a Justicar for a lifetime (as well as hundreds of other people), and even Archons and Templars have told us that the Inner Circle of the Camarilla contains at least one Sabbat infiltrator.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not the infiltration part that strains credulity, it's the &quot;Mrs. Doubtfire&quot;-ing that does. There's just no way a single vampire maintains two high-profile, but more importantly high-maintenance (i.e. they have to do their jobs regularly and be seen by others doing that job on a regular basis), roles posted up in high-security, high surveillance locations in two different countries on opposite sides of a continent. Let alone for centuries, without anyone (who matters) getting at least suspicious even before taking into account the gaping holes in either's stories, which just beg for heightened scrutiny.<br /> <br /> Granted, a Gangrel is better-suited than any other clan save the necromancers for off-the-grid travel -- you're never, <i>ever</i> beating a master necromancer with a ferryman spirit slave. Gangrel by default can shift into animal form and earth meld -- a borderline methuselah stretches that to its very limits, considering they can shift into more exotic and even mythical forms, and travel while earth melded. But, Gangrel <i>safe</i> travel isn't <i>fast</i> travel, let alone in modern nights where the technological alternatives are passenger jets capable of near-sonic or supersonic flight.<br /> <br /> Other vampires who successfully execute high-level infiltrations, including those you cited, only had to preserve a single cover that allowed (or required) them to be sedentary. That's just not the case here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T21:43:29-07:00","id":1542092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541018-best-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1542076#post1542076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not the infiltration part that strains credulity, it's the &quot;Mrs. Doubtfire&quot;-ing that does. There's just no way a single vampire maintains two high-profile, but more importantly high-maintenance (i.e. they have to do their jobs regularly and be seen by others doing that job on a regular basis), roles posted up in high-security, high surveillance locations in two different countries on opposite sides of a continent. Let alone for centuries, without anyone (who matters) getting at least suspicious even before taking into account the gaping holes in either's stories, which just beg for heightened scrutiny.<br /> <br /> Granted, a Gangrel is better-suited than any other clan save the necromancers for off-the-grid travel -- you're never, <i>ever</i> beating a master necromancer with a ferryman spirit slave. Gangrel by default can shift into animal form and earth meld -- a borderline methuselah stretches that to its very limits, considering they can shift into more exotic and even mythical forms, and travel while earth melded. But, Gangrel <i>safe</i> travel isn't <i>fast</i> travel, let alone in modern nights where the technological alternatives are passenger jets capable of near-sonic or supersonic flight.<br /> <br /> Other vampires who successfully execute high-level infiltrations, including those you cited, only had to preserve a single cover that allowed (or required) them to be sedentary. That's just not the case here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, vampire ancients can and do use body doubles, Astral Projection, and Dominate 5.<br /> <br /> It's highly UNLIKELY but not impossible.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga<