edy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T11:26:40-07:00","id":1542259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541018-best-antagonist-in-v-tm?p=1542230#post1542230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't go wrong with disliking the Tremere clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>The best Tremere chraracters I've seen being played, were by Players who really disliked the Clan and thought of them as nothing more than a rigid, sniveling, traitorous and treacherous, hierarchy of spies and mercenaries; who will use every dirty trick in the book to remove a threat to their blood sorcery monopoly, and lie through their teeth about others having done something, and refusing to accept they did anything wrong. Just like corporations and war criminals! <br /> <br /> So, funnily enough, the Tremere are best played by Players who want to play as the Clan, but find them detestable in some way. So you really play out those sides of them. <br /> Same thing with Ventrue, although they do fall into their own lies of grandeur and dignity, while the Tremere are more cynical.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T11:53:35-07:00","id":1542261,"title":"","content":"In terms of generic antagonists?<br /> <br /> I've gotten a lot of mileage out of Assamite hitmen, mortal gangbangers, the Sabbat in general, lupines, zombies, and of course, hunters (including both mortal hunters and Imbued, as well as Senshi)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T14:52:48-07:00","id":1542274,"title":"","content":"My clan the Malkavians make good unpredictable antagonists with their mental issues and horrific uses of the Disciplines. How do you counter a threat that thinks outside the box and try tactics that you wouldn't consider?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coron